# Pinned tools, Scoop-bucket style: everything Portable-Codespaces needs that
# apt does not provide. `codespace setup` downloads each tool for this host's
# architecture into apps/<tool>/<version>/, refuses it unless the sha256
# matches, and points apps/<tool>/current at it.
#
# One line per tool, version and architecture, whitespace-separated:
#
#   tool  version  arch  sha256  url
#
# arch is amd64, arm64, or `any` for an architecture-independent download.
# Bump a version by replacing its lines, never by editing a URL alone: the
# sha256 must come from the publisher (SHASUMS256.txt, the GitHub release
# digest), not from hashing whatever the URL serves today.

# Node.js, only to run the devcontainer CLI. The newest LTS line; the CLI
# needs >= 20. Hashes: https://nodejs.org/dist/v26.13.1/SHASUMS256.txt
